    jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_blowup_2026-11-27, P3, closed, "stale: FIXED by p3sweep4-20261127 (u8 admitted to the large_scalar_fill runtime-fill path; [0u8; 64M] 61s/14.2GB to 3s flat); spec RED 3/4 to GREEN 4/4 2026-11-27", doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_blowup_2026-11-27.md, 1, doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_blowup_2026-11-27.md, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_blowup_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 seen on aarch64 DGX with seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b while timing 16 MB inputs. No library code uses constant-size large literals; perf drivers switched to runtime sizes."
    jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_blowup_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: root cause: hir/lower/expr/collections.rs:141 lower_array_repeat large_scalar_fill guard deliberately excluded u8, so constant-N u8 repeats expanded into N-element HIR literals (runtime-count repeats were already fine; the MIR byte-packed bulk fill lower_u8_array_repeat_expr already existed). Fix: added TypeId::U8 to the large_scalar_fill match (u64 still unrolls - documented rt_array_repeat readback divergence); counts < 256 and side-effecting values still unroll. Timings on the scratch build: [0u8; 16M] 2-11s/0.7-3.5GB to 2-4s flat; [0u8; 64M] 26-61s/14.2GB to 3s flat; element values verified before/after. Spec jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_budget (SIMPLE_BINARY convention, process_run_timeout budgets) RED 3/4 (64M blows its budget unpatched) to GREEN 4/4 in 5.6s; function_tests assert fill vs unrolled; jit_u8_repeat_literal_copy_push 11/11 + 4/4 incl the existing byte-array-new-len assertions. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_budget_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/hir/lower/tests/function_tests.rs"

